1
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,840
Somehow, it'll work out.

2
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:59,940
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:04,500
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:11,940
Look, even the Akanel is burning.

5
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll all work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? Got it, got it.

7
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,460
Once you understand,
gather up and follow me.

8
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:04,480
Thank you for watching.

9
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,920
The range will double!

10
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:06,840
Whoa!

11
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:10,360
Listen up, watch closely!
Two bombing runs at once!

12
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:17,560
Wow! Just like Kankichi!

13
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:20,160
That's right! I'm a genius, after all!

14
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:21,200
Hey!

15
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:24,440
So it was you lot who pulled this prank!

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,840
Tonpe! Chikichi! Run!

17
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:30,720
Look! Batsu!

18
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:32,240
Batankā!

19
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:36,740
No kids' portable shrine this year, then.

20
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:38,820
It's falling apart everywhere.

21
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:40,600
It's dangerous if it
breaks while being carried.

22
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,620
We've sent it for repairs so many times.

23
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:46,200
Let's order a new one for next year.

24
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:49,340
The neighborhood kids carry it so roughly.

25
00:02:49,340 --> 00:02:51,960
They always bang it into
each other like it's a fight.

26
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,740
It's probably Gin-san's son from Sukudania.

27
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:57,220
That's what shortened the shrine's life.

28
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:05,940
I wonder what they were
doing inside the shrine.

29
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:08,840
Hey, Kankichi! The lock isn't on!

30
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:23,720
Yes! We're so lucky to face the Miyata Island mikoshi!
I saved a spot to carry it!

31
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:28,900
This spot's mine!
I grabbed the best spot all by myself!

32
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:32,100
This spot's always been mine every year!

33
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:33,140
It's me!

34
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:35,080
No way, this spot's mine!

35
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,600
No, back off!

36
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:38,840
Back off, back off!

37
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,360
Come on, come on, come on!

38
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,820
Aaaaah!

39
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:44,920
I-it broke!

40
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:46,420
W-what do we do now?

41
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:48,840
It fell over because you pushed it!

42
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:51,180
No, it's Tombei's fault!

43
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:54,400
It's your fault for cutting
in line in the first place!

44
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,480
This isn't the time for that!

45
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:58,520
We have to do something about this mikoshi!

46
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,660
It's already broken, so what do we do?

47
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,920
Is there any way to fix it?

48
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:06,380
Right, let's swap it with
the one from Hacchōme!

49
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:19,820
The Hacchōme mikoshi is exactly like ours.

50
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,280
If we swap them quietly, no one will notice.

51
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:25,220
But Hacchōme is quite a long way off.

52
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:28,000
As long as we swap them before morning,
we'll be fine.

53
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:31,140
Even so,
it's too heavy for just three of us.

54
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:36,000
Is the shrine still far?

55
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:36,860
Not yet.

56
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,020
Shall we take a break, Kankichi?

57
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:40,940
My shoulders feel like
they're about to fall apart.

58
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:44,420
No, we'll miss the deadline before morning!

59
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,260
I won't carry a mikoshi
again for another ten years!

60
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:52,560
Right, let's take a shortcut.

61
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:57,300
If we go this way,
we'll arrive an hour earlier.

62
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,820
The Hacchōme shrine is at the bottom of the embankment,
after all.

63
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:02,380
But I wonder if the train will come.

64
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:05,760
The first train shouldn't be running yet,
so it should be fine.

65
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:10,560
What?

66
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:36,740


67
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:49,680
Damn it,
all that hard work went down the drain!

68
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:54,880
So it was truly too late,
like a festival after it's over.

69
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:58,120
You really shouldn't do
such dangerous things.

70
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:01,040
I just want to say,
good kids shouldn't copy this.

71
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:06,240
Festivals were a huge event when we were kids,
you know.

72
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:09,219
It was fun, wasn't it?
Getting pocket money and

73
00:06:09,269 --> 00:06:12,220
looking for things we wanted
under the acetylene lamps.

74
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,500
Acetylene lamps?

75
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:14,660
I don't know.

76
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:17,680
Nakagawa and Reiko's generation
probably wouldn't know them.

77
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:21,560
At the stalls, they used lamps instead
of electric lights for illumination.

78
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,671
Come to think of it,
we'd often get too close,

79
00:06:23,721 --> 00:06:25,980
and there was always someone
who'd singe their hair.

80
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:30,200
I still remember that
flame's color and smell.

81
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:33,660
Ryo-chan, you really are a festival lover,
aren't you.

82
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:34,420
Well, yeah.

83
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:37,500
Speaking of which, where's the Chief today?

84
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:38,540
He's off duty.

85
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:42,020
But he said he'd come to the festival later

86
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:44,440
with Hiromi-san and Daisuke and the others.

87
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:48,820
And Honda-san and Komachi-chan and
the others said they'd be coming too.

88
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:52,080
Hmph, and here we are, busy with the keirin.

89
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:54,160
So everyone's just off to the festival

90
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:10,340
Behind-the-back strike!
Underhand strike! Double aerial shot!

91
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,060
Wow! That's amazing, Ryo-san!

92
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:20,400
Heh-heh! This is easy, easy!

93
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:24,160
Where's the patrol? I'm busy!

94
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:26,780
You've completely gone back to being a kid.

95
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:28,566
Don't count on Ryo-chan,

96
00:07:28,616 --> 00:07:30,820
let's do the patrol just the two of us.

97
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:31,420
Yeah.

98
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,880
Wow, that's amazing!

99
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:35,960
How does that work?

100
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:38,400
Now, watch closely, okay?

101
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:42,660
Look, from right here, a ten-yen coin...

102
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:44,840
Whoa, how's he doing that?

103
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:46,440
That's amazing, mister!

104
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:48,500
Show us more!

105
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:49,600
Show us, show us!

106
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:53,560
Alright, alright, then watch closely.

107
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:55,960
Now, what's going to disappear this time?

108
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:58,420
Wow.

109
00:07:58,980 --> 00:07:59,700
Wow!

110
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:01,480
That's certainly

111
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:05,340
It's my wallet after all!

112
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,340
When did that happen!

113
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:07,800
That's an amazing magic trick!

114
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:09,660
That wasn't magic at all.

115
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:10,960
That was pickpocketing.

116
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:14,860
Excuse me, could you show me that once more?

117
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:17,049
Sure thing, Officer,

118
00:08:17,099 --> 00:08:19,320
it's just a simple kids' trick.

119
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:20,820
Well then, you little rascals,

120
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:22,180
Bye-bye, see ya!

121
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:23,876
You there,

122
00:08:23,926 --> 00:08:26,840
Anzaam,
eating it like this is the best, right?

123
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:31,200
That's not something a uniformed
police officer should be doing.

124
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:33,660
How's this?

125
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:36,320
It might be too much for cavemen.

126
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:38,560
What, two bug-eyed goldfish?

127
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,600
What did you say?

128
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,080
Well, they look just alike, don't they?

129
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:44,680
That flashy yukata makes you look like a
bug-eyed goldfish from a goldfish-scooping stall.

130
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:46,500
What is it?

131
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:48,380
You have zero appreciation for beauty.

132
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:49,900
Senpai.

133
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:51,120
Good evening.

134
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,040
No, Otohime is here too.

135
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:56,240
You two shouldn't get
too cozy with each other.

136
00:08:56,240 --> 00:09:01,380
It'd be an eyesore for you two, who still
haven't gotten a boyfriend after all this time.

137
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:02,180
What?

138
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:05,740
I don't want to hear that from a single,
lecherous middle-aged man.

139
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:08,860
Shall we go pray at the shrine, Nana-chan?

140
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:09,320
Yeah.

141
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:12,080
Let's draw fortunes.

142
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:12,980
Maybe it'll be great luck.

143
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:15,760
Damn it!

144
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:17,440
But

145
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,840
Damn it!

146
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:23,160
Now, what should I eat next?

147
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,800
Auntie, two hot ones, please.

148
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:31,020
You're on duty,
and you've still got quite the appetite

149
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:43,440
Pucha... wow, Hiromi-san, you've grown up too, Daisuke-kun.
Sakura-chan looks just like Hiromi-san, which is a relief.
If she looked like some stubborn old man, I couldn't bear to look at her.

150
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:50,480
What was that? Well, Chief, at least be quiet during the festival.
That's right, Papa.

151
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:50,720
Pop!

152
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,620
Ah, yeah, that's right.

153
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:55,080
Grandpa, let's go yo-yo fishing!

154
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,500
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

155
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:58,080
Listen, Ryotsu.

156
00:09:58,080 --> 00:10:00,140
The festival is a prime place to make money.

157
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:01,820
Be very careful.

158
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:03,660
Yes, yes, I understand.

159
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:06,280
Looks like even the Chief
can't refuse his grandchild.

160
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,300
Yeah.

161
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:11,680
Whoa, whoa,
you'll get hurt if you rush like that.

162
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:13,860
Hurry, hurry, Grandpa!

163
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:15,300
Sorry.

164
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:16,280
Watch out.

165
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:18,580
That one...

166
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,060
Let's hurry.

167
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:22,020
Uh.

168
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:26,060
No way, that guy...

169
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:28,240
No, that can't be right.

170
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,760
Grandpa, honestly!

171
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,600
Sorry, sorry!

172
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,280
Come on, let's go!

173
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:34,280
Hey, hey, no running!

174
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,440
Hey, wait, goldfish!

175
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:38,260
I'll arrest you!

176
00:10:38,260 --> 00:10:39,720
Hold on a second!

177
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:40,560
Yah!

178
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:42,940
I told you to stop!

179
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,260
Okay, this one...

180
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:45,360
Come on!

181
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:49,060
You have nowhere left to run!

182
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:50,840
Yah!

183
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:53,500
Got you!

184
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:54,680
Aaah!

185
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:58,200
It has the character from
Nana-chan's manga on it.

186
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,140
I'll have that one, please.

187
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:02,200
Thanks! Ours is delicious!

188
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:04,880
I'll throw in a discount! Three million yen!

189
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:05,560
Thank you.

190
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:08,120
It's a shame to eat it.

191
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:08,800
Yeah, it is.

192
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:11,940
Ken-dono, where did I put the wallet?

193
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,320
Checking for any coin box thieves.

194
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:18,160
I've got to keep a close watch here.

195
00:11:22,020 --> 00:11:24,600
With me keeping a sharp
eye on things like this,

196
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:27,260
everyone can enjoy the
festival with peace of mind.

197
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,960
I'm really something, aren't I?

198
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,200
What have you gone and done?

199
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:36,300
Damn.

200
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:37,840
We can still make it if we hurry.

201
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:38,700
Put it back right away!

202
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:39,920
Pickpocket!

203
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:45,020
Senpai, my wallet's gone.

204
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:45,480
What?

205
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:47,480
Mine's gone too.

206
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:50,340
My wallet's gone somewhere.

207
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:53,860
That had a six-month commuter pass in it!

208
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:55,380
Senpai!

209
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:56,200
It's a pickpocket!

210
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:58,440
Right, split up and catch him!

211
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:00,800
There's a pickpocket!

212
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,880
Daddy's a pickpocket!

213
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:03,980
What?

214
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:08,160
No way... It can't be.

215
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:20,800
My wallet's gone.

216
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:21,760
I've been pickpocketed.

217
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:22,360
What?

218
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:25,680
So the culprit must be nearby!

219
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:27,380
You there, man!

220
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:28,580
Hey, stop right there!

221
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:30,180
Like I'd let you get away!

222
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:35,340
You bastard!

223
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:38,740
You're under arrest for
being caught in the act!

224
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:40,160
Hand over what you stole.

225
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,800
Let go of me!

226
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:44,360
Let go? Like hell I will!

227
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:45,920
You pickpocketing bastard!

228
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,700
(cicadas chirping)

229
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:51,380
Bakabon, you fool! Ryo-tour!

230
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:53,300
Then, Chief!

231
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:57,300
But why would the Chief be a pickpocket?

232
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:59,040
I would never pick anyone's pocket!

233
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:01,600
But you ran away, Chief, so I just assumed!

234
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,700
I just needed to use the toilet!

235
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:06,840
Me...

236
00:13:09,449 --> 00:13:12,440
I've found him this time!

237
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:14,400
Kura! Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

238
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,380
Sorry! I left it there!

239
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,920
Damn, I lost him.

240
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,240
He definitely came this way.

241
00:13:24,660 --> 00:13:26,160
Where the hell did he go?

242
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:30,540
Ryotsu.

243
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,180
Ow.

244
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:35,820
What are you doing, here of all places?

245
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:37,320
Chief.

246
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:41,660
Did a pickpocket run this way?

247
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:42,500
Pickpocket?

248
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:46,667
No, I've been gazing at this
sacred tree the whole time,

249
00:13:46,717 --> 00:13:47,960
and nobody came by.

250
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:51,740
That's strange. Where did he run off to?

251
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:54,500
Get it together. Go search over there.

252
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,060
Right, right.

253
00:13:57,380 --> 00:13:58,780
You can come out now.

254
00:13:58,780 --> 00:13:59,500
Whoa!

255
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:02,300
Long time no see, Karasawa.

256
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:05,080
Mr. Ohara.

257
00:14:05,570 --> 00:14:07,620
It's been 15 years... no, maybe more.

258
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:10,540
Back when Hiromi was still in the
lower grades of elementary school.

259
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:13,060
Thank you for your help back then.

260
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:19,120
How's business been at
your factory since then?

261
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,900
You seem to have lost a bit of weight.

262
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,200
I retired from my job last year when
I hit the mandatory retirement age.

263
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:25,740
That's good.

264
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:28,060
So you've kept working hard all this time.

265
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:34,240
Grandpa, Hiromi,
are you going to scoop up the goldfish?

266
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,800
Hurry, hurry!

267
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:38,680
There, there.

268
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:45,840
That man is a habitual pickpocket,
Shogoro Karasawa.

269
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:48,220
Grandpa! Grandpa, come on!

270
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:52,920
No, you're holding on too tight.
That hurts, Hiromi, doesn't it?

271
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,200
Sorry, sorry.

272
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:00,520
He's gone.
We can only arrest a pickpocket in the act.

273
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:01,860
Damn it.

274
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,200
Where did Karasawa go?

275
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:07,460
There he is!

276
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:13,620
1, 2, 3!

277
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:15,880
Aww, it tore!

278
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:19,680
Whoa, I got one!

279
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:21,980
Look, Papa, Papa!

280
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:23,140
Papa?

281
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,120
So close

282
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,580
I saw that, Karasawa.

283
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:30,980
You...

284
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:34,020
We're the police. Your time is up.

285
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:36,220
Dad.

286
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:37,260
Masaru.

287
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:41,080
There's something fun going on over there.
Let's go see.

288
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:44,600
Yeah, later. Go on ahead.

289
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,580
Let's go now, Dad!

290
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:48,580
Just go on ahead already.

291
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:51,260
Well, I'll go on ahead.

292
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:53,260
Hurry up and come, Dad.

293
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,600
Sorry for all the trouble.

294
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:03,580
We wouldn't want the kids to see this,
would we?

295
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:09,760
Daddy, look! Look, I did it!

296
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,080
Good job, Hiromi.

297
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:14,640
Daddy has some business with this man here.

298
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:17,900
Hiromi's a good girl,
so you can wait by yourself, right?

299
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,580
Bye-bye, take care.

300
00:16:23,880 --> 00:16:27,240
So when you get out,
I'll stand as your guarantor.

301
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:30,480
If you love your children,
get yourself an honest job.

302
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:48,900
Don't you ever come back here again,
Karasawa.

303
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:51,880
Halt!

304
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:00,400
Good work. You've got a job.

305
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:02,500
They want you to start as early as tomorrow.

306
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:05,620
That's great. A fresh start from the city.

307
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:07,960
Thank you so much.

308
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,020
I'll never make a mistake again.

309
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:15,440
Yes, you mustn't make
Masaru and your wife cry.

310
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:16,820
Promise me.

311
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:22,180
I was deeply moved by your kindness back then,
Mr. Ohara.

312
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:26,240
No, it's the result of your own effort.

313
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:29,980
What happened to your wife?

314
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:33,720
We were both working,
and two years ago she suddenly passed away.

315
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:37,640
I see. I've reminded
you of something painful.

316
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:39,240
And now?

317
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:42,740
I'm imposing on a married couple's home now.

318
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:44,700
That time...

319
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:46,360
Come quickly, Daddy!

320
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:50,920
But life hasn't been very kind to us,
you know.

321
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:56,460
Masaru's company went under, you see.

322
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,360
On top of that, their lives became unstable,

323
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:03,100
and with me having no income,
they'd have to look after me too.

324
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:07,520
At my age,
I can't even find a new job easily.

325
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:10,080
And it's hard to say that I'm
just lounging around the house.

326
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,200
I see.

327
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:13,280
Grandpa!

328
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,180
Daisuke.

329
00:18:15,180 --> 00:18:17,640
Hey, Grandpa, buy me a robot!

330
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,260
You promised!

331
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:22,000
I know, I know. Later.

332
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:25,320
I'll come later, so go to your mom.

333
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:26,760
Okay, but you promised!

334
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,440
That's my grandson, Daisuke.

335
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:32,360
And there's his little sister, Sakura.
They're two siblings.

336
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:37,020
Does your son Masaru and
his wife have any children?

337
00:18:37,860 --> 00:18:41,560
One boy, about the same age.

338
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,080
I see.

339
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,780
They must be adorable.

340
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:48,840
They say grandchildren are so precious you could keep them in your eye,
and it's true.

341
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:51,760
Just being with them puts my mind at ease.

342
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:56,560
Even though I'm their grandfather, I
can't buy them anything for their birthday.

343
00:18:57,500 --> 00:19:00,040
Who's this you know, Kei-chan?

344
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:02,080
I happened to spot him earlier.

345
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:05,260
He told the kids it was a magic trick,

346
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,420
but it wasn't magic at all.
It was a pickpocketing trick.

347
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:12,400
I understand how he feels.

348
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:15,700
But money and things

349
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:18,060
aren't the only way to show
love to a grandchild, surely.

350
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:20,360
Don't you think so?

351
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:25,600
I wonder where he went.
I'd recognize his face right away, though.

352
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:29,320
Nakagawa, Reiko,
have you found the pickpocket?

353
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:33,040
Kei-chan says she saw
someone who looks like him.

354
00:19:33,420 --> 00:19:35,940
There are so many people, we can't find him.

355
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:39,460
Nakagawa, pickpockets are
arrested in the act, you know.

356
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:42,900
If he gets away or ditches the evidence wallet,
it's all over.

357
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:45,960
Understood. I won't let him get away.

358
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:48,560
Rather than goods or money,

359
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:52,180
I'll teach you the rules of the world through experience,
for example.

360
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:54,880
What's right and what's wrong.

361
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:58,040
Keeping promises is one of them.

362
00:19:59,580 --> 00:20:00,320
A promise.

363
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:04,920
Thank you very much.

364
00:20:05,840 --> 00:20:07,480
I'll never pick another pocket again.

365
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:10,880
You mustn't make your wife or Masaru cry.

366
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,060
Promise me.

367
00:20:12,860 --> 00:20:13,860
Chief Ohara.

368
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:15,860
I won't say any more than that.

369
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:22,880
I wonder who Chief Ohara is talking to.

370
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:27,840
What's wrong, Nakagawa?

371
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:30,680
Chief Ohara, who is this man?

372
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:34,000
He's an acquaintance of mine, but...

373
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,820
The chief's acquaintance?

374
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:37,500
Kei-chan.

375
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:41,100
Never mind that, everyone's making a
fuss about a pickpocket, a pickpocket.

376
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:43,120
Did a pickpocket really show up?

377
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:44,780
It's true.

378
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:48,200
Mr. Honda's and Komachi-chan's
wallets were stolen too.

379
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,300
It might be a mistake, you know.

380
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:52,940
Tell them to search again thoroughly.

381
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:53,860
Chief.

382
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:56,260
It's because they wore unfamiliar yukata.

383
00:20:56,260 --> 00:20:59,320
They've probably
forgotten where they put it.

384
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:05,980
Nakagawa

385
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:11,140
Nakagawa!

386
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:16,120
Tell the other victims to double-check
whether their wallets were really stolen.

387
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:17,340
Y-yes, sir!

388
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:20,840
I know what's going on.

389
00:21:22,580 --> 00:21:22,980
Mm-hm.

390
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:27,800
That's him!

391
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,140
Pickpocket, you're busted!

392
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:33,320
I got the food!

393
00:21:35,180 --> 00:21:38,580
Damn it,
so he hid them in a place like this!

394
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:40,520
Senpaaai!

395
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,600
Here, check them carefully!

396
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:46,220
This is my wallet!

397
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:46,980
That's mine!

398
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:47,960
There's one of mine too!

399
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:48,440
Thank goodness!

400
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:51,620
See? That's the irrefutable evidence!

401
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:52,760
Dammit!

402
00:21:53,420 --> 00:21:54,840
Good work, Ryotsu!

403
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:55,720
Senpai!

404
00:21:58,920 --> 00:22:00,720
Just as I thought, only mine is missing!

405
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:08,360
Excuse me.

406
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:10,620
Mind if I take a quick look?

407
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:11,720
Nakagawa...

408
00:22:15,060 --> 00:22:15,860
Found it.

409
00:22:15,860 --> 00:22:18,720
The money and my commuter
pass are both safe!

410
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:19,560
Thank goodness.

411
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:21,940
Even if it's the Chief, I...

412
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:24,440
Well, the Chief was right after all.

413
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:26,360
Terai's was just some careless klutz who...

414
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:27,860
Right, Nakagawa?

415
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:31,200
I'm really sorry for the trouble.

416
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:32,280
No, no.

417
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:35,820
It's Grandpa!

418
00:22:35,820 --> 00:22:36,940
Dad.

419
00:22:36,940 --> 00:22:38,460
Grandpa!

420
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:40,100
You guys...

421
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:46,040
Thank goodness. You disappeared without a word,
so I was worried.

422
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:49,680
Masaru said you've always loved festivals,

423
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:51,120
so he figured you'd probably be here.

424
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:54,340
Dad, I've got a new job lined up.

425
00:22:54,980 --> 00:22:58,400
The conditions are better than before,
and I'm so excited I could shake.

426
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:01,700
That's great. That's really great.

427
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:05,360
Grandpa, today we're having sushi,
your favorite.

428
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:08,480
Tadashi loves it too, doesn't he.

429
00:23:10,020 --> 00:23:11,220
Tadashi

430
00:23:11,220 --> 00:23:14,640
Yes. It's written with the character for
"honest," and it's read Tadashi.

431
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:17,900
What a good name. Well then, Ohara-san.

432
00:23:19,260 --> 00:23:20,600
Bye-bye!

433
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,440
Grandpa.

434
00:23:24,440 --> 00:23:28,040
I feel like I met that
man when I was little.

435
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:30,605
Ahaha, that's right,

436
00:23:30,655 --> 00:23:32,460
he's an old friend of mine.

437
00:23:32,460 --> 00:23:33,435
Come on,

438
00:23:33,485 --> 00:23:36,820
the Chief gets teary far too easily,
doesn't he.

439
00:23:36,820 --> 00:23:40,520
Well, they say there are no
bad people among festival lovers.

440
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:43,320
Ryotsu, you...

441
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:44,820
Heh heh.

442
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:46,126
You, you idiot,

443
00:23:46,176 --> 00:23:50,360
just because you love festivals
doesn't mean you can neglect your work.

444
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:52,720
Hurry up and take that man away.

445
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:54,460
Yes, yes. Hey, let's go.

446
00:24:47,060 --> 00:24:49,240
Thank you for your hard work.

447
00:24:49,460 --> 00:24:53,380
We were all kids once, but everyone forgets.

448
00:24:54,580 --> 00:24:57,580
Politicians with their self-important faces,

449
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,940
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

450
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:06,440
Turn that corner, come and see.

451
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:11,620
You can meet everyone, everyone!

452
00:25:13,980 --> 00:25:16,300
Over there is Kameari.

453
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:19,580
Surely there's Kameari.

454
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:24,920
Everyone, come on over to our town!

455
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:26,340
Thank you.

456
00:25:29,780 --> 00:25:32,600
Thank you all for supporting me for so long.

457
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:36,880
This time I really did get
fired from the police force.

458
00:25:37,400 --> 00:25:40,380
Reiko, why are you working so hard for me?

459
00:25:42,660 --> 00:25:44,620
Next time: goodbye, Ryo-san!

460
00:25:44,620 --> 00:25:47,120
Reiko, marry me!

461
00:25:48,420 --> 00:25:50,720
Over there is Kameari.

462
00:25:51,700 --> 00:25:54,060
Surely there's Kameari.

463
00:25:55,180 --> 00:25:59,220
Everyone, come on over to our town!

464
00:26:00,140 --> 00:26:00,780
Thank you.

